<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ SPORT - England to bowl in rain-shortened game.</title>
<headline>NZ SPORT - England to bowl in rain-shortened game.</headline>
<dateline>NEW PLYMOUTH 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>England won the toss and decided to field in a rain-shortened one-day match against a New Zealand Academy side in New Plymouth on Friday.</p>
<p>The game was reduced to 46 overs a side after rain delayed the start of play and pushed the start time back to 1.15 p.m.</p>
<p>Match rules allow for the contest to be reduced to 25 overs a side before it would have to be cancelled.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
